within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L01X_OtherAntineoplasticAgents.L01XX02_Asparaginase;
model Asparaginase_Hoeben2026_PD_tv
  "linear exposure-response sweep — Hoeben_2026 :: TV (tumor volume)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Interfaces.PartialExposureResponseSweep(
    E0 = 152,      // [mm3]
    Emax = 0, EC50 = 1,      // unused by a line
    exposure_per_s = 1);
  parameter Real slope = 3.22   "[L/IU/h × 10−5]";
equation
  response = E0 + slope*exposure;
  // family_inferred: the record's model family is disease_progression; read from the parameters: a slope and no Emax — linear
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 1000, Interval = 2),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Asparaginase_Hoeben2026_PD_tv</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Hoeben E et al., <i>European journal of drug metabolism and pharmacokinetics</i> 2026 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1007/s13318-026-01010-4\">doi:10.1007/s13318-026-01010-4</a>) — tumor volume [mm3] against plasma asparaginase activity IU/L — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: linear.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =        152 mm3      drug-free response (baseline) (W0, Q324)
  slope =       3.22 L/IU/h × 10−5 change in response per unit of exposure (slp, Q335)</pre><p>The algebra is <code>response = E0 + slope*exposure</code>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one IU/L of plasma asparaginase activity per second of simulated time: there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 152   (drug-free)</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Hoeben_2026: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Asparaginase_Hoeben2026_PD_tv;
